Subject: order obstacles by item creation, not by address
Upstream-file: pcbnew/router/pns_item.h (ITEM), pcbnew/router/pns_node.h (OBSTACLE::operator<)
Why: NODE::OBSTACLES is a std::set<OBSTACLE> ordered by the items'
 addresses. NearestObstacle takes the first of equally near obstacles in
 that order, and TOPOLOGY::AssembleCluster builds its walkaround cluster in
 it, so the same request routed in two processes could answer differently
 (macOS: 2 of 12 runs of one pic_programmer route moved a corner by 1 nm;
 the fixture suite's replay check caught it). Every ITEM now carries a
 serial from a process-wide counter (a copy gets a new one; an assignment
 keeps the target's, so no two live items share one: review r3 P-1), and
 OBSTACLE orders by the serials, keeping the addresses only as the last,
 unreachable, tie-break.
 Relative creation order is the same in every run, whatever the counter's
 start, so the order is too.
Upstream: yes, as a determinism fix (KiCad's own router-replay tooling
 would benefit); not yet proposed.

